"""Direct question-design review of meditation and prāṇāyāma."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

MEDITATION = """history_origins|A Named Meditation Practice in Its Sources|Where does one specified practice first appear in surviving texts?|Distinguish source date, later teaching, and present form.
famous_examples|A Well-Known Meditation Program Examined|What does one widely cited program include beyond meditation?|Compare manual, teacher training, participant group, and measured outcome.
hidden_stories|Teachers and Participants Beyond the Founder|Whose work and experience are missing from one practice history?|Use consented accounts and dated institutional records.
beginner_explainers|Which Meditation Do We Mean?|How does one named method define attention, setting, and purpose?|Attribute the method to its community; distinguish it from broad wellness branding.
advanced_concepts|Practice, Comparator, and Outcome|How can a study isolate the effect of a particular meditation program?|Specify components, comparison group, adherence, follow-up, and harms.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Effect With Uncertain Cause|What cannot a small meditation study establish about a reported outcome?|Examine expectancy, selection, co-interventions, and missing follow-up.
technology_innovation|A Meditation App Under Evaluation|Does one app reproduce the studied practice and support user safety?|Compare content, supervision, privacy, engagement, and evidence.
people_personalities|A Teacher's Documented Influence|What did one teacher change in a named meditation lineage?|Use writings, recordings, and students' accounts with attribution.
major_events|A Practice Moves into Healthcare|What changed when one program entered a clinical setting?|Compare original aim, adapted curriculum, evidence, and oversight.
how_it_works|A Meditation Session as Taught|How do teachers describe the stages and purpose of one public method?|Document the local curriculum without giving a therapeutic protocol.
rise_fall|Changing Use of a Practice|Why did participation in one program grow or decline?|Check enrollment definitions, institutions, media, and access.
then_vs_now|A Traditional Practice and a Clinical Adaptation|Which elements were retained or removed in one adaptation?|Compare source tradition, modern manual, teachers, and stated goals.
future_developments|The Next Study Needed|Which research question would clarify benefit or harm for a defined group?|State comparator, outcomes, safety reporting, and follow-up.
myths_vs_facts|A Universal Meditation Benefit?|Does a sweeping claim fit evidence for the exact method and population?|Distinguish clinical findings from personal and spiritual testimony.
documentary_stories|One Program's Evidence Trail|How did a meditation program move from teaching to public health claims?|Follow manuals, trials, reviews, marketing, and corrections.
text_source|A Meditation Passage in Context|What does one named text actually say about a practice?|Check original language, edition, surrounding passage, and commentary.
interpretive_lineages|Two Readings of Contemplation|How do named traditions understand a similar meditation term differently?|Attribute each interpretation and avoid combining methods.
lived_practice|A Practitioner's Own Purpose|What does one consented practitioner say the practice means in daily life?|Separate personal meaning from evidence of clinical efficacy.
ritual_sequence|Meditation Within an Observance|Where does one contemplative segment occur in a named tradition?|Document local public practice and respect restricted elements.
language_translation|A Word Rendered as Meditation|What gets lost when a source term is translated simply as meditation?|Compare grammar, historical context, and living usage.
regional_variants|A Method in Two Settings|How does one named method change between communities or clinics?|Compare teachers, curriculum, cultural setting, and goals.
art_and_devotion|Contemplation in Art or Poetry|How does one artwork portray a named meditative ideal?|Distinguish artistic expression from a literal practice manual.
community_memory|Remembering a Teacher or Practice|How does lineage memory compare with dated teaching records?|Attribute memory and explain gaps without dismissing it.
ethics_in_context|Consent and Vulnerability in Instruction|What safeguards does one program use for participants who report distress?|Read policy, adverse-event reporting, and participant accounts; give no clinical advice.
source_and_history|A Practice's Textual History|What evidence links an older source to a current meditation method?|Trace named teachers and texts; do not infer continuity from a shared label.
encounter_and_exchange|A Method Crosses Traditions|How was one practice adapted across religious or secular settings?|Trace documented transmission, permissions, and changes in purpose.
contemporary_voice|A Teacher and a Participant Disagree|What do different present participants say the practice is for?|Represent consented views without treating either as universal.
field_textual_lineage|A Contemplative Instruction Across Editions|How does wording vary in one source tradition?|Compare witnesses, translation, and commentary.
field_regional_practice|A Local Meditation Community|How is one method taught and supported in a named place?|Use consented accounts and institutional context.
field_translation_choice|Two Renderings of a Practice Term|How do translation choices change what a reader thinks to do?|Compare source context without issuing instructions.
field_ritual_context|Contemplation in a Local Rite|How do practitioners explain its place within one observance?|Respect access rules and distinguish local practice from broad claims.
field_community_interpretation|A Community Defines Its Meditation|How do members explain aims, boundaries, and variation?|Attribute accounts and include internal differences."""

PRANAYAMA = """history_origins|Breath Practice in a Named Source|What does one dated text say about prāṇāyāma in its own framework?|Separate textual description from later technique and clinical claim.
famous_examples|A Widely Taught Breath Method|How is one named method described by its teaching lineage?|Compare source text, present curriculum, variation, and safety boundaries.
hidden_stories|Teachers Behind Breath Practice|Whose instruction and adaptation shaped one community's practice?|Use consented teacher accounts and dated materials.
beginner_explainers|What Prāṇāyāma Names|How do different yoga traditions use the term prāṇāyāma?|Distinguish breath regulation, philosophical explanation, and clinical intervention.
advanced_concepts|Testing a Breath Intervention|How can a trial define one breathing method precisely enough to evaluate it?|Specify pacing, duration, supervision, comparator, population, and adverse events.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Physiological Claim in Question|Which part of a claimed mechanism remains untested for a named method?|Compare laboratory measures with patient outcomes and study limits.
technology_innovation|A Breathing Device or App|Can a device reproduce a studied method safely and accurately?|Check measured pacing, user feedback, privacy, and validation.
people_personalities|A Teacher's Adaptation|How did one named teacher change a documented breath curriculum?|Compare earlier source, teaching record, and later interpretations.
major_events|Breath Practice Enters a Program|What changed when one method was adapted for a school or clinic?|Compare aims, screening, instructor training, and evidence.
how_it_works|Documenting a Taught Method|Which components distinguish one named breath practice from another?|Describe source and study protocols without instructing viewers to perform it.
rise_fall|A Technique's Popularity Over Time|Why did one breath method gain or lose institutional support?|Use course records, publications, public claims, and safety reports.
then_vs_now|A Textual Practice and a Modern Class|What changed in the teaching context of one breath method?|Compare texts, teacher lineage, curriculum, and participant aims.
future_developments|A Safer Evidence Study|What trial design could clarify outcomes and harms for a defined group?|State supervision, exclusions, adverse-event capture, and follow-up.
myths_vs_facts|Breathwork as a Cure?|Does one advertised health claim match evidence for the exact method and condition?|Check study design, population, harms, and current guidance.
documentary_stories|One Breath Claim's Paper Trail|How did a traditional description become a modern therapeutic promise?|Trace source, trial, marketing, and regulator or guideline response.
text_source|A Prāṇāyāma Passage in Context|What does a named text prescribe or explain within its broader system?|Cite edition, chapter, translation, and later commentary.
interpretive_lineages|Two Accounts of Prāṇa|How do named lineages interpret the role of breath differently?|Present each conceptual framework without asserting a medical mechanism.
lived_practice|A Practitioner's Breath Practice|What does one consented account reveal about meaning and routine?|Separate experience from clinical efficacy and avoid technique instructions.
ritual_sequence|Breath Practice Within a Rite|Where does a named community place prāṇāyāma in its observance?|Document public sequence and respect restricted material.
language_translation|Prāṇa in Translation|How do translations of prāṇa change a reader's understanding?|Compare original contexts and avoid equating it automatically with a physiological measure.
regional_variants|One Method Across Two Lineages|How do comparable breath practices differ in teaching and meaning?|Specify lineage, place, source, and instructor context.
art_and_devotion|Breath in a Text or Image|How is breathing represented symbolically in one tradition?|Distinguish symbolic meaning from clinical function.
community_memory|A Lineage Remembers a Breath Method|How does oral teaching history compare with dated manuals?|Attribute both and state evidence gaps.
ethics_in_context|Safety and Screening|How does one program address distress, dizziness, or other adverse experiences?|Read published protocols and adverse-event reports; provide no personal guidance.
source_and_history|Transmission of a Breath Text|How do manuscripts and later teaching records connect one method across time?|Avoid assuming identical technique from a repeated name.
encounter_and_exchange|Breath Method in a New Setting|What changed when one lineage's practice moved into wellness or care?|Compare consent, purpose, supervision, and evidence.
contemporary_voice|A Teacher Explains Boundaries|How does one qualified teacher describe when a method is inappropriate?|Use attributed educational interview and verify current safety guidance.
field_textual_lineage|A Breath Passage Across Witnesses|What variants appear in one source passage?|Compare manuscript base, edition, and translation.
field_regional_practice|Local Breath Teaching|How is one method taught in a named community?|Document curriculum and participant safeguards without publishing instructions.
field_translation_choice|A Technical Breath Term|Which translation best fits one bounded passage?|Compare grammar, commentary, and practice context.
field_ritual_context|Prāṇāyāma in Observance|What role does a named breath element have in one local rite?|Ask practitioners, respect restrictions, and avoid replication detail.
field_community_interpretation|One Lineage's View of Breath|How do members explain purpose and variation within a method?|Attribute their views and avoid universal claims."""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("278", "278_meditation", MEDITATION,
                  "Named meditation traditions and adaptations, practice aims, transmission, clinical evidence, participant experience, and safety.",
                  "specified primary texts and translations, teaching manuals, registered trials and systematic reviews, current clinical guidance, adverse-event reports, and consented accounts",
                  "Name the exact method, lineage or program, population, and outcome. Attribute spiritual claims; do not present an anecdote as clinical proof or provide therapeutic instructions. Include possible harms and current guidance.")
    revise_domain("279", "279_pranayama", PRANAYAMA,
                  "Named prāṇāyāma traditions, breath concepts, teaching contexts, clinical claim evaluation, and participant safety.",
                  "specified source texts and translations, teaching curricula, registered trials and systematic reviews, current guidance, adverse-event reports, and consented accounts",
                  "Distinguish traditional prāṇa concepts from measured physiology and exact breathing protocols. Provide no breath-holding or forceful-breathing instructions or personal treatment advice; verify safety for the studied population.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
